<Article slug="best-standing-desks-singapore">
<p>An electric standing desk is one of the bigger home office purchases you'll make, and in Singapore the choice usually comes down to three routes: buy a complete desk from a big-box store, buy a frame and add your own top, or pay more for a premium all-in-one. We picked one well-known option for each route and compared what their makers and local retailers actually publish.</p>

<h2>Quick picks</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Desk</th><th>Best for</th><th>Price at time of writing (28 Oct 2026)</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>IKEA MITTZON sit/stand, electric</td><td>Most people who want a complete desk, delivered</td><td>around S$599 to S$659 (IKEA Family price)</td></tr>
<tr><td>FlexiSpot E7 Pro frame</td><td>DIYers who want a sturdy frame and their own top</td><td>around S$500 for the frame (Howfine)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Secretlab MAGNUS Pro</td><td>Premium, clean-cable setups with a metal top</td><td>check Secretlab SG</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<Product id="ikea-mittzon-sitstand" rank={1} verdict="Best all-round pick: a complete dual-motor desk with a long guarantee.">
<p>MITTZON is IKEA's current electric sit/stand range. IKEA Singapore lists it as a <strong>dual-motor</strong> desk with a <strong>10-year guarantee</strong>, and it comes in several sizes: 120x60, 120x80, 140x60, 140x80 and 160x80 cm, with white, birch, black-stained ash and walnut veneer tops.</p>
<p>When we checked on 28 October 2026, IKEA Family prices ran from about S$599 (120x60 cm) to S$659 (160x80 cm), a S$50 saving on the regular prices. IKEA's page showed the deal valid until August 2027 or while stock lasts. Product pages showed average shopper ratings of about 4.5 to 4.8 out of 5, from fairly small numbers of reviews (around 13 to 20 per variant).</p>
<p><strong>Why it suits Singapore homes:</strong> the 60 cm-deep versions fit narrow HDB study rooms, and you can see one in person at an IKEA store before you buy.</p>
<p><strong>Watch out for:</strong> fewer published motor and load specs than the specialist brands, so if you plan heavy monitors or a lot of gear, check the product page details first.</p>
</Product>

<Product id="flexispot-e7-pro" rank={2} verdict="Best frame for a custom setup: high published load rating.">
<p>The E7 Pro is one of FlexiSpot's best-known frames. FlexiSpot's official (US) site lists it at <strong>440 lb (about 200 kg) maximum static load</strong>, a height range of about 25" to 50.6" (roughly 64 to 129 cm), widths from 47.2" to 80", and noise under 50 dB. FlexiSpot says it is rated for 30,000+ lift tests and has an extended cable tray.</p>
<p>FlexiSpot doesn't run a Singapore checkout on its global site, so we looked at local sellers. Singapore office furniture supplier Howfine listed the <em>E7 Pro frame</em> at around S$500 on 28 October 2026, with local delivery and a 12-month warranty from Howfine.</p>
<p><strong>Watch out for:</strong> the S$500 listing is for the <em>frame</em>, so budget extra for a desktop. The long frame warranty FlexiSpot advertises on its US site may not apply to a local reseller purchase, so confirm warranty terms with the seller.</p>
</Product>

<Product id="secretlab-magnus-pro" rank={3} verdict="Premium pick: metal desktop and built-in cable management.">
<p>Secretlab is a Singapore company, and the MAGNUS Pro is its electric standing desk. It's sold directly through Secretlab SG in a standard size and a larger XL size. Its main selling points are an all-metal desktop and a built-in cable management system, which suits people who want a very tidy setup.</p>
<p>Secretlab changes its prices and bundles often, so check the current price on the Secretlab SG page. It has generally cost more than the other two options here.</p>
<p><strong>Watch out for:</strong> a metal top means you're tied into Secretlab's accessory ecosystem for things like magnetic cable covers. Check the dimensions against your room before you buy.</p>
</Product>

<h2>How to choose a standing desk in Singapore</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Measure your room first.</strong> Many HDB study rooms suit a 120 or 140 cm wide desk. Leave room behind the chair to roll back.</li>
<li><strong>Dual motors are worth it</strong> if you'll load the desk with monitors, a PC tower or a monitor arm. They generally lift more smoothly and evenly than single-motor frames.</li>
<li><strong>Check the height range against your own height.</strong> Standing height should put your elbows at about 90°. Taller users should check the maximum height carefully.</li>
<li><strong>Delivery and assembly.</strong> Standing desks are heavy. Check whether the seller delivers to your floor and whether assembly is included or extra.</li>
<li><strong>Warranty from <em>whom</em>?</strong> Buying from a local reseller can mean different warranty terms from the brand's global site.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Bottom line</h2>
<p>If you want one purchase that just works, the <strong>IKEA MITTZON</strong> is the easiest recommendation: complete, dual-motor, a 10-year guarantee and a showroom you can visit. If you'd rather pick your own top and want a highly rated frame, look at the <strong>FlexiSpot E7 Pro</strong>. If budget matters less than looks and cable tidiness, the <strong>Secretlab MAGNUS Pro</strong> is the premium choice.</p>
</Article>
